comment_data.body:
Thanks for the issue! I can reproduce (nicely detailed steps, by the way!)

As far as my investigation can tell, the behavior of 'mini.completion' is somewhat expected. Here is why.

TL;DR: `vue_ls` returns a completion item with `textEdit` containing "outdated" range that needs to be replaced. This happens when typing more than one character if the first 'textDocument/completion' request was incomplete (hence new request is made after the next key press).

---

More details. I reproduced the issue with created file 'tmp.vue' containing the suggested text. The following patch was used for logging information (applied for commit 126ce3328c78399dcff58272f6f540a373b62a75):

<details><summary>Patch for 'mini.completion' logging</summary>

```diff
diff --git a/lua/mini/completion.lua b/lua/mini/completion.lua
index bbf3d84..c557917 100644
--- a/lua/mini/completion.lua
+++ b/lua/mini/completion.lua
@@ -1188,6 +1188,8 @@ H.lsp_get_filterword = function(x) return x.filterText or x.label end
 H.lsp_item_compare = function(a, b) return (a.sortText or a.label) < (b.sortText or b.label) end

 -- Completion -----------------------------------------------------------------
+_G.log = {}
+
 H.make_completion_request = function()
   local current_id = H.completion.lsp.id + 1
   H.completion.lsp.id = current_id
@@ -1200,6 +1202,16 @@ H.make_completion_request = function()
   -- filtered with one `base`. Anyway, the most common situation is with one
   -- attached LSP client.
   local cancel_fun = vim.lsp.buf_request_all(buf_id, 'textDocument/completion', params, function(result)
+    local res_logged = vim.deepcopy(result)
+    res_logged[1].result.items = vim.tbl_filter(
+      function(x) return x.label == 'background-color' end,
+      res_logged[1].result.items
+    )
+    table.insert(
+      _G.log,
+      { 'textDocument/completion', cur_line = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line(), result_trunc = res_logged }
+    )
+
     if not H.is_lsp_current(H.completion, current_id) then return end

     H.completion.lsp.status = 'received'
@@ -1368,6 +1380,15 @@ H.make_lsp_extra_actions = function(lsp_data)
     local from, to = { init_base.lnum, init_base.col }, vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)
     -- NOTE: actual base string should not be relevant here, only byte count
     local prefix = string.rep('x', init_base.length)
+    table.insert(_G.log, {
+      'before restore state',
+      {
+        init_base = vim.deepcopy(init_base),
+        to = vim.deepcopy(to),
+        cur_line = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line(),
+        prefix = prefix,
+      },
+    })
     pcall(vim.api.nvim_buf_set_text, 0, from[1] - 1, from[2], to[1] - 1, to[2], { prefix })
     to = { from[1], from[2] + init_base.length }

@@ -1506,6 +1527,8 @@ H.info_window_lines = function(info_id)
   H.info.lsp.status = 'sent'

   local cancel_fun = H.client_request(client, 'completionItem/resolve', lsp_data.item, function(err, result, _)
+    table.insert(_G.log, { 'completionItem/resolve', vim.deepcopy(result) })
+
     -- Don't do anything if there is other LSP request in action
     if not H.is_lsp_current(H.info, current_id) then return end

```

</details>

Typing `b`, `a`, `c`, `<C-n>`, `<CR>` (slowly) accepted the "background-color" snippet item and reproduced the issue. Here is the output of logging with manually added `--` comments with details:

<details><summary>Value of `_G.log`</summary>

```lua
{ { "textDocument/completion",
    cur_line = "\t  b",
    result_trunc = { {
        -- Results from vue_ls
        result = {
          isIncomplete = true,
          itemDefaults = {
            -- Default range says that it replaces single "b" letter
            editRange = {
              start = { line = 5, character = 3 },
              ["end"] = { line = 5, character = 4 },
            }
          },
          items = { {
              -- ...
              insertTextFormat = 2,
              kind = 10,
              label = "background-color",
              sortText = "d_a1",
              tags = {},
              textEdit = {
                newText = "background-color: $0;",
                -- Explicit range also says that it replaces single "b" letter
                range = {
                  start = { line = 5, character = 3 },
                  ["end"] = { line = 5, character = 4 },
                }
              }
            } }
        }
      }, {
        -- Results from ts_ls
        result = {
          isIncomplete = false,
          items = {}
        }
      } }
  }, { "textDocument/completion",
    -- Line has increased by one character, BUT both default and item's edit
    -- ranges say that they remove single character (first "b")
    cur_line = "\t  ba",
    result_trunc = { {
        result = {
          isIncomplete = true,
          itemDefaults = {
            editRange = {
              start = { line = 5, character = 3 },
              ["end"] = { line = 5, character = 4 },
            }
          },
          items = { {
              -- ...
              insertTextFormat = 2,
              kind = 10,
              label = "background-color",
              sortText = "d_a1",
              tags = {},
              textEdit = {
                newText = "background-color: $0;",
                range = {
                  start = { line = 5, character = 3 },
                  ["end"] = { line = 5, character = 4 },
                }
              }
            } }
        }
      }, {
        result = {
          isIncomplete = false,
          items = {}
        }
      } }
  }, { "textDocument/completion",
    -- Line has increased AGAIN by one character, BUT both default and item's
    -- edit ranges STILL say that they remove single character (first "b")
    cur_line = "\t  bac",
    result_trunc = { {
        result = {
          isIncomplete = false,
          itemDefaults = {
            editRange = {
              start = { line = 5, character = 3 },
              ["end"] = { line = 5, character = 4 },
            }
          },
          items = { {
              -- ...
              insertTextFormat = 2,
              kind = 10,
              label = "background-color",
              sortText = "d_a1",
              tags = {},
              textEdit = {
                newText = "background-color: $0;",
                range = {
                  start = { line = 5, character = 3 },
                  ["end"] = { line = 5, character = 4 },
                }
              }
            } }
        }
      }, {
        result = {
          isIncomplete = false,
          items = {}
        }
      } }
  }, { "completionItem/resolve", {
      client_id = 1,
      -- ...
      insertTextFormat = 2,
      kind = 10,
      label = "background-color",
      sortText = "d_a1",
      tags = {},
      textEdit = {
        newText = "background-color: $0;",
        range = {
          -- Information is unchanged during resolve
          start = { line = 5, character = 3 }
          ["end"] = { line = 5, character = 4 },
        }
      }
    } }, { "before restore state", {
      -- The state before applying a snippet is correctly restored (just uses
      -- "xxx" instead of "bac"). The `textEdit` says that the first character
      -- needs to be replaced with the snippet, NOT all three. So some extra
      -- characters will remain (they should be *after* inserted text, but that
      -- is a 'mini.completion' issue of not accounting edge case of text edit
      -- be not at cursor at this point).
      --
      -- I'd say that the correct behavior from `vue_ls` here is to update
      -- `textEdit` on every 'textDocument/completion' request.
      cur_line = "\t  background-color",
      init_base = { col = 3, length = 3, lnum = 6 },
      prefix = "xxx",
      to = { 6, 19 }
    } } }
```

</details>

Here is a demo:

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ddedca3f-92bd-4e0e-b938-5837c3b6214d

So in the end, `vue_ls` in all three requests returned an item with `textEdit` saying that only a first "b" should be replaced with a snippet. So inserting a snippet does exactly that (after some shenanigans with "xxx" restoring state) which results in extra leftover characters (if not "xx", it would have been "ac").

Technically, this also violates [LSP specification](https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/#completionItem), part about `textEdit`: "*Note:* The range of the edit must be a single line range and it must contain the position at which completion has been requested.". The second and third time completion was requested to the right of the provided `textEdit`.

---

Closing as "looks like an upstream issue and 'mini.completion' behaves as expected; completely not sure why 'nvim-cmp' doesn't have this issue".

---

An interesting observation in this use case is that 'mini.completion' doesn't ensure correct cursor position before inserting snippet ([here](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/126ce3328c78399dcff58272f6f540a373b62a75/lua/mini/completion.lua#L1393)). It assumes that `textEdit` (if supplied) covers current cursor position or is adjacent on the left. I think extra `vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, { to[1], to[2] })` before replacing text might be a good idea. Need to take a closer look.
